{
 "cells": [
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "# SU(3) adjoint chain, L = 2 — final twisted Baxter/SoV matching\n\nThis notebook is self-contained and keeps only the final construction.\n\n1. Build the two-site adjoint monodromy and commuting transfer matrices with a unimodular diagonal twist.\n2. Diagonalize a generic linear combination numerically, weight sector by weight sector; build the product reference covector/vector and the normalized physical scalar product.\n3. Feed every transfer-matrix eigenvalue into the direct and dual Baxter equations.\n4. Form the product right reference wave function $\\Psi_B^{\\rm ref}$.\n5. Build the $6\\times6$ FSoV determinant (rows $(\\alpha,i,j)$, full contour, periodic insertion for $\\alpha=2$), divide by $c_A^{\\rm ref}=\\prod_\\alpha c^{\\rm ref,L=1}_A(\\theta_\\alpha)$ and by $\\Psi_B^{\\rm ref}$, vacuum-normalize once, and compare the complete $64\\times64$ matrices for both L=1 branches.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* ---- 1. gl(3) adjoint representation and the L=2 twisted chain. ---- *)\nClearAll[\n    ps,\n    dim,\n    J0,\n    Jp,\n    Jm,\n    JJ,\n    rep2,\n    dsite,\n    dchain,\n    idsite,\n    Esite1,\n    Esite2,\n    Etot2,\n    EElocal,\n    thetaValues,\n    hValue,\n    zTwist,\n    Tmon,\n    qminor2,\n    subsets2,\n    qcoeff2,\n    Tcoeff2,\n    nu1L2,\n    nu2L2,\n    nu3L2,\n    qdetL2,\n    u\n];\n\nps[rr_] :=\n    ps[rr] =\n    Block[\n        {res = Prepend[rr, #]& /@ Tuples[Table[Range[rr〚1, i + 1〛, rr〚1, i〛], {i, 1, Length[rr〚1〛] - 1}]]},\n        If[Length[res〚1, 1〛] == 1, Reverse @ Sort @ res, Reverse @ Sort @ Flatten[ps /@ res, 1]]\n    ];\ndim[rr_] := dim[rr] = Length[ps[{rr}]];\nJ0[k_][pat_] := J0[k][pat] = Sum[pat〚k, i〛, {i, 1, k}] - Sum[pat〚k - 1, i〛, {i, 1, k - 1}];\nJp[k_][pat_] :=\n    Jp[k][pat] =\n    -Sum[\n        Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k + 1, j〛 + j, {j, Range[k + 1]}]\n        / Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k, j〛 + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} → pat〚k, i〛 + 1]],\n        {i, 1, k}\n    ];\nJm[k_][pat_] :=\n    Jm[k][pat] =\n    Sum[\n        Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k - 1, j〛 + j, {j, Range[k - 1]}]\n        / Product[pat〚k, i〛 - i - pat〚k, j〛 + j, {j, Complement[Range[k], {i}]}] v[ReplacePart[pat, {k, i} → pat〚k, i〛 - 1]],\n        {i, 1, k}\n    ];\nJJ[k_, l_, rr_] :=\n    JJ[k, l, rr] =\n    Which[\n        k == l,\n        DiagonalMatrix[J0[k] /@ ps[{rr}]],\n        l == k + 1,\n        Transpose @ Table[Coefficient[Jp[k][ps[{rr}]〚i〛], v[#]]& /@ ps[{rr}], {i, Length[ps[{rr}]]}],\n        l == k - 1,\n        Transpose @ Table[Coefficient[Jm[l][ps[{rr}]〚i〛], v[#]]& /@ ps[{rr}], {i, Length[ps[{rr}]]}],\n        l > k + 1,\n        JJ[k, k + 1, rr].JJ[k + 1, l, rr] - JJ[k + 1, l, rr].JJ[k, k + 1, rr],\n        l < k - 1,\n        JJ[k, k - 1, rr].JJ[k - 1, l, rr] - JJ[k - 1, l, rr].JJ[k, k - 1, rr]\n    ];\n\nrep2 = {2, 1, 0};\ndsite = dim[rep2];\ndchain = dsite^2;\nidsite = IdentityMatrix[dsite];\nEElocal[i_, j_] := EElocal[i, j] = JJ[i, j, rep2];\nEsite1[i_, j_] := Esite1[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[EElocal[i, j], idsite];\nEsite2[i_, j_] := Esite2[i, j] = KroneckerProduct[idsite, EElocal[i, j]];\nEtot2[i_, j_] := Esite1[i, j] + Esite2[i, j];\n\nthetaValues = {1 / 3, -8 / 57};\nhValue = 1;\n(* Unimodular twist: the scalar product needs z1 z2 z3 = 1, otherwise the\n   pairing Q^j Q_i keeps a leftover (z1 z2 z3)^(u/h) factor. *)\nzTwist = {5 / 2, 7 / 3, 6 / 35};\n\nTmon[i_, j_][x_] :=\n    Sum[\n        ((x - thetaValues〚1〛) KroneckerDelta[i, k] IdentityMatrix[dchain] - hValue Esite1[k, i]).(\n            (x - thetaValues〚2〛) KroneckerDelta[k, j] IdentityMatrix[dchain] - hValue Esite2[j, k]\n        ),\n        {k, 3}\n    ];\nqminor2[II_] :=\n    Expand @ Sum[Signature[s] Dot @@ Table[Tmon[II〚s〚k〛〛, II〚k〛][u - (k - 1) hValue], {k, Length[II]}], {s, Permutations[Range[Length[II]]]}];\nsubsets2[a_] := Subsets[Range[3], {a}];\nDo[With[{m = qminor2[II]}, Do[qcoeff2[II, k] = Coefficient[m, u, k], {k, 0, 2 Length[II]}]], {II, Join @@ (subsets2 /@ Range[3])}];\nTcoeff2[a_, k_] := Tcoeff2[a, k] = Sum[(Times @@ zTwist〚II〛) qcoeff2[II, k], {II, subsets2[a]}];\n\nnu1L2[x_] := Product[x - th - 2 hValue, {th, thetaValues}];\nnu2L2[x_] := Product[x - th - hValue, {th, thetaValues}];\nnu3L2[x_] := Product[x - th, {th, thetaValues}];\nqdetL2[x_] := nu1L2[x - 2 hValue] nu2L2[x - hValue] nu3L2[x];\n\nGrid[\n    {\n        {\"site dimension\", dsite},\n        {\"chain dimension\", dchain},\n        {\"parameters {theta1,theta2,h,z}\", {thetaValues, hValue, zTwist}},\n        {\"twist is unimodular\", Times @@ zTwist == 1},\n        {\n            \"all coefficients of T1,T2 commute\",\n            And @@ Flatten @ Table[Tcoeff2[a, k].Tcoeff2[b, l] == Tcoeff2[b, l].Tcoeff2[a, k], {a, 2}, {b, 2}, {k, 0, 2 a}, {l, 0, 2 b}]\n        },\n        {\n            \"T3 is the quantum determinant\",\n            Expand[Sum[Tcoeff2[3, k] u^k, {k, 0, 6}] - qdetL2[u] IdentityMatrix[dchain]] == ConstantArray[0, {dchain, dchain}]\n        }\n    },\n    Frame → All,\n    Alignment → Left\n]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
